@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{gptel-plus.el} extends @uref{https://github.com/karthink/gptel, gptel}, the Emacs package for interfacing with large language models.  It adds cost awareness, context persistence, and quality-of-life improvements that are useful when working with paid LLM APIs on a regular basis.

The development repository is on @uref{https://github.com/benthamite/gptel-plus, GitHub}.

The package provides four groups of functionality:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Cost estimation and tracking.}  Before sending a request, @samp{gptel-plus} estimates its cost and displays it in the header line.  After a request completes, it parses the response log to report the exact cost.  When a request exceeds a configurable cost threshold, it asks for confirmation before proceeding (@ref{Cost estimation}).

@item
@strong{Context persistence.}  The gptel context (files added via @code{gptel-context-add-file}) is ephemeral by default: it is lost when you kill the buffer.  @samp{gptel-plus} can save and restore context to and from the file itself, as an Org property or a Markdown file-local variable (@ref{Context persistence}).

@item
@strong{Context file management.}  A dedicated buffer lists all context files sorted by size, with a dired-like interface for flagging and removing files in bulk.  This is especially helpful when you need to trim a large context to reduce costs (@ref{Context file management}).

@item
@strong{Automatic mode activation.}  @samp{gptel-plus} can automatically enable @code{gptel-mode} when you open a file that contains gptel data, so that you can resume a conversation without manually toggling the mode (@ref{Automatic mode activation}).
@end itemize

The package requires Emacs 29.1 or later and @samp{gptel} 0.7.1 or later.

