@node Manual installation
@section Manual installation

Clone the repository somewhere on your @code{load-path} and load the package:

@lisp
(require 'gptel-plus)
@end lisp

@node Installation with use-package
@section Installation with use-package

The following snippets show how to install @samp{gptel-plus} with the most common package managers.  Choose whichever one matches your setup.

@lisp
;; with vc (built-in, Emacs 29+)
(use-package gptel-plus
  :vc (:url "https://github.com/benthamite/gptel-plus"))

;; with elpaca
(use-package gptel-plus
  :ensure (:host github :repo "benthamite/gptel-plus"))

;; with straight
(use-package gptel-plus
  :straight (:host github :repo "benthamite/gptel-plus"))

;; with quelpa
(use-package gptel-plus
  :quelpa (gptel-plus :fetcher github :repo "benthamite/gptel-plus"))
@end lisp

@node User options
@chapter User options

All user options belong to the @code{gptel-plus} customization group, which is itself a child of the @code{gptel} group.

@menu
* Cost estimation parameters::
@end menu

@node Cost estimation parameters
@section Cost estimation parameters

@vindex gptel-plus-calculate-cost
@vindex gptel-plus-tokens-per-word
@vindex gptel-plus-tokens-in-output
@vindex gptel-plus-cost-warning-threshold

The user option @code{gptel-plus-calculate-cost} controls whether cost estimation and tracking are active.  When set to @code{nil}, no cost information is computed or displayed.  The default value is @code{t}.

The user option @code{gptel-plus-tokens-per-word} specifies the approximate number of tokens per word, used for converting word counts into token counts when estimating input costs.  The default value is @samp{1.5}.  If your typical prompts use a language other than English, or if you frequently include code (which tends to have a higher token-to-word ratio), you may want to increase this value.

The user option @code{gptel-plus-tokens-in-output} specifies the assumed number of tokens in the model's response, used for estimating output costs.  The default value is @samp{100}.  If your typical interactions produce longer responses, increase this value to get more accurate cost estimates.  For a conservative upper bound, you could set it to the value of @code{gptel-max-tokens}, though this will overestimate costs for most requests.

The user option @code{gptel-plus-cost-warning-threshold} sets the dollar amount above which @samp{gptel-plus} prompts for confirmation before sending a request (@ref{Cost warning}).  The default value is @samp{0.15} (fifteen cents).  Set it to @code{nil} to disable the warning entirely.  The type accepts either a number or @code{nil}.

